{# The pictogram an element carries, from the theme library or from the media
   library.

   Expected variables:
     - icon        : an `iw_theme_icon_picker` value, as resolved for the website
     - item        : or the data holding the flat icon fields, for project
                     templates still on the icon-picker.xml fragment.
                     Deprecated with the fragment.
     - class       : extra classes for the icon itself
     - blockPrefix : BEM prefix of the calling block, for a hook of its own

   Returns nothing at all when no icon was picked, so a caller can test the
   output before opening a wrapper around it.

   Parameters, continued:
     - recolor : repaint a media SVG with the surrounding colour. On by the
       caller that paints its own background - a button - and off everywhere
       else.

   A library icon is always inlined and always follows the colour around it:
   Heroicons carry no colour of their own, so there is nothing to preserve.
   Which colour that is comes from `--iw-icon-color`, which a block sets for its
   own slot - accent on a card, the label colour on a button.

   A media file is the editor's own, so it keeps its colours by default: a brand
   logo on a card has to stay that brand's. Only `recolor` overrides that, and
   only for an SVG, where the mask can fill a shape with the current colour. A
   bitmap is never masked - a mask keeps the shape and turns an avatar into a
   silhouette.

   The size travels as a custom property rather than a class: the field offers a
   handful of steps today and enumerating them in CSS would mean keeping a copy
   of that list in step. #}
{#- Two shapes. `icon`: an `iw_theme_icon_picker` field as resolved for the
    website ({custom, icon, weight, media, size}), the media already loaded. `item`:
    the flat fields of the icon-picker.xml fragment, the media an id to load. -#}
{% set picker = icon is defined and icon is iterable ? icon : null %}
{% set iconCustom = picker ? (picker.custom ?? false) : (item.iconCustom ?? false) %}
{% set iconName = iconCustom ? '' : (picker ? picker.icon|default('') : item.icon|default('')) %}
{% set iconWeight = picker ? picker.weight|default('outline') : 'outline' %}
{% set iconSize = picker ? picker.size|default('') : item.iconSize|default('') %}
{% set iconClass = ('iw-icon ' ~ (class|default('')) ~ (blockPrefix|default('') ? ' ' ~ blockPrefix ~ '__icon' : ''))|trim %}

{% set iconMediaUrl = '' %}
{% set iconMediaVector = false %}
{% if iconCustom %}
    {% if picker %}
        {% set iconMediaResolved = picker.media ?? null %}
    {% else %}
        {% set iconMediaResolved = item.iconMedia.id is defined ? sulu_resolve_media(item.iconMedia.id, app.request.locale) : null %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if iconMediaResolved is not null %}
        {% set iconMediaVector = 'image/svg+xml' == iconMediaResolved.mimeType|default('') %}
        {% set iconMediaUrl = iconMediaVector
            ? iconMediaResolved.url
            : iconMediaResolved.thumbnails['50x50']|default(iconMediaResolved.url) %}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{%- if iconName and iw_sulu_tailwind_theme_has_icon(iconName, iconWeight) -%}
    {{ iw_sulu_tailwind_theme_icon(iconName, iconWeight, {
        class: iconClass,
        width: 24,
        height: 24,
        style: iconSize ? '--iw-icon-size: ' ~ iconSize ~ 'px' : false
    }) }}
{%- elseif iconMediaUrl and iconMediaVector and recolor|default(false) -%}
    <span class="{{ iconClass }} iw-icon--mask"
          style="--iw-icon-media: url('{{ iconMediaUrl }}'){{ iconSize ? '; --iw-icon-size: ' ~ iconSize ~ 'px' : '' }}"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
{%- elseif iconMediaUrl -%}
    {#- Decorative: whatever it stands beside already says it. -#}
    <img class="{{ iconClass }} iw-icon--image" src="{{ iconMediaUrl }}" alt=""
         width="24" height="24" loading="lazy"
         {%- if iconSize %} style="--iw-icon-size: {{ iconSize }}px"{% endif %}>
{%- endif -%}
